2) what is lamda exp?
      * Lamda exp is a anonomous function.
            - anonoums means(name less) the function which is not having a name such type of name less function is called anonomous function. 
            - not having modifiers  (public, private,....)
            - not having return type
        ex :
              () -> { S.O.P ("Hello");
                   or
              () -> S.O.P("Hello");     -> when contains only one statement

        ex :
              (int a, int b) -> {S.O.P(a+b);
                        or
              ( a , b) -> S.O.P(a+b);       -> when contains only one statement

        ex :
              ( String s) -> {return s.length();}
                          or
               (s)->  s.length();       -> when contains only one statement
                           or
                  s -> s.length();        -> when contains only one statement

      Characteristics / properties of lamda expression
      1) A lamda exp can take any no of parameters
            ex :
                  () -> s.o.p("hello");
                  (s)-> s.length();
                  (a,b) -> s.o.p(a+b);
      2) If mulitple parameters present then these parameters should be repeated with,
            ex: (a,b) -> s.o.p(a+b);
      3) If only one parameter available then parenthesis are optional
                  (s)->s.lenbgth(); => s->s.length();
      4) Usually we can specify the type of parameter of compilter expect the type based on context, then we can remove type {Type Inference}
            ex:
                  (int a, int b) -> s.o.p(a+b); => (a,b)->s.o.p(a+b);
      5) Similar to method body, lamda exp body can contain any number of statements. If multiple statements are there then we should enclose within curly braces.
      ex: 
            () -> {
                        statement 1;
                        statement 2;
                        statement 3;
                  }
        * If body contains only one statement then curly braces are optional
              () -> s.o.p("Helloo");

      6) If lamda exp return something then we can remove return keyword;
            s-> s.length();
3) LAmda exp uses
      1- To enable functional programming in java.
      2- Write more readable , maintainable and concise code.
      3- To use API's very easily & effecitvely
      4- To enable parallel programming
      * LISP programming lang used 1st to use lamda exp


4) Functional Interface
      If the interface contain only single abstract method is called funtional Interface.
      Runnable -> conatins only run() method
      Callablle -> contains only call() method
      ActionListener -> conatins only actionPerformed()
      Comparable -> contains only compareTo() 

            ex:
                  interface Interface
                  {
                        public void m1(); //abstract method 
                        default void m2();
                        default void m3();
                        {
                        }
                        public static void m3()
                        {
                        }
                  }

5) Functional Interface wrt Inheritance
      1) If an interface extends Functional Interface and child interface doesnt contain any abstract method, then child interface is always Functional Interface.
            Ex :
                  @FunctionalInterface
                  interface p
                  {
                        public void m1(0;
                  }
                  @FunctionalInterface
                  interface C extends P
                  {
                  }
      2) In the child interface , we can define exactly same parent interface abstract method.
            Ex:
                  @FunctionalInterface
                  interface p
                  {
                        public void m1();
                  }
                  @FunctionalInterface
                  interface C extends P
                  {
                        public void m1();
                  }
      3) In the child interface we cant define any new abstract methods otherwise we will get Complier Exception.
            Ex:
                  @FunctionalInterface
                  interface P
                  {
                        public void m1();
                  }
                  @FunctionalInterface 
                  interface C extends P
                  {
                        public void m2();
                  }

             This gives compiler Exception @FunctionalInterface annotation, multiple non-overriding abstract methods found in interface 'C'
      4)
            Ex:
                  @FunctionalInterface
                  interface P
                  {
                        public void m1();
                  }
                  interface C extends P
                  {
                        public void m2();
                  }
                        

6) Code without lamda Expression and with lamda exoression
      Without lamda Expression
      ------------------------
            interface Interf
            {
                  public void m1();
            }
            Class Demo implements Interf
            {
                  public void m1()
                  {
                        S.O.P("m1() method implementation");
                  }
            }
            Class Test
            {
                  public static void main(String[] args)
                  {
                        Interf i = new Demo();
